# Trivy ignore list for go-codec.
#
# The gate has two parts (conventions/devops.md §8):
#
#   trivy fs     — SOURCE scan of the shipped Go module, failing on
#                  CRITICAL/HIGH. examples/ is skipped; it is demo code that
#                  never ships to a consumer of the library.
#   trivy image  — the CI/tooling image this repo builds (golang:<stable>-
#                  bookworm plus protoc), failing on FIXABLE CRITICAL/HIGH.
#                  Unfixed Debian advisories are excluded there because no
#                  rebuild can action them; a fixable one means the base is
#                  stale and is a real finding.
#
# Add specific advisory IDs below ONLY when a finding is confirmed
# not-applicable or unfixable, with a one-line justification AND the date it
# was accepted. An entry without both is a defect.
#
# Example:
# CVE-XXXX-XXXXX  # 2026-01-01 <reason this advisory does not apply to go-codec>
